UPDATE companies SET description='In La Apparel operates from Los Angeles and Orange County, California, as a vertically integrated apparel manufacturer focused on made-in-USA production. The company runs two factories, including a knitting mill in the Los Angeles fashion district, and employs a small team to manage design, development, and production for private-label clients.

The company provides full-service private-label manufacturing covering design consulting, pattern making, grading, marking, cutting, sewing, fabric and garment dyeing, printing, embroidery, sublimation, heat transfer, and specialty decorations such as deboss, burnout, and reflective transfers. Its in-house knitting mill produces fabrics in cotton, synthetic, viscose/modal, polyester, melanges, organic, and slub yarns, while also offering organic and sustainable options. Production scales from low-minimum-order samples to large-volume runs, with packaging and fulfillment handled on-site.

Clients span the fashion industry, corporate and uniform programs, promotional products, and entertainment production studios creating costumes for motion pictures, commercials, and television. The company works directly with independent designers, established brands, and artists, offering end-to-end development from concept through retail-ready shipment.

In La Apparel differentiates itself through a sweatshop-free, vertically integrated model that keeps all manufacturing domestic, emphasizing customer service and quality control at every stage. The firm highlights its ''Organic Zone'' for 100% organic apparel, fast turnaround times, and the ability to process orders of any quantity, positioning itself as a one-stop partner from fabric development to final delivery.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Private label apparel manufacturing", "Cut and sew", "Knitting", "Fabric dyeing", "Garment dyeing", "Printing", "Embroidery", "Sublimation", "Heat transfer", "Deboss/emboss", "Cotton burnout", "Reflective transfer/print", "Pattern making", "Grading", "Marking", "Sample development", "Pre-production sampling", "Packaging", "Fulfillment", "Design consulting", "Fabric development", "Organic fabric production", "Costume design for entertainment"], "industries": ["Fashion", "Corporate", "Uniform", "Promotional", "Entertainment"], "materials": ["Cotton", "Synthetic", "Viscose/Modal", "Polyester", "Melanges", "Organic cotton", "Slub", "Bamboo", "Tencel", "French Terry", "Mesh", "Modal Spandex", "Fleece", "Sweater Knit", "Hacci"], "equipment": ["Garber System", "knitting mill"], "volume": "Small batch to large scale; low MOQ", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated with in-house knitting mill", "Low minimum order quantities", "Sweatshop-free, made-in-USA production", "Full-service from design to fulfillment", "Organic and sustainable fabric options"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Los Angeles, California -> db", "Employee count: 5 -> db", "Vertically integrated with in-house knitting mill -> /about", "Two factories in Los Angeles and Orange County -> /", "Services: design, development, production, consulting -> /", "Processes: knitting, dyeing, printing, cutting, sewing, decorating, packaging, fulfillment -> /about", "Industries: fashion, corporate, uniform, promotional, entertainment -> /, /about", "Materials: cotton, synthetic, viscose/modal, polyester, melanges, organic, slub, bamboo, tencel -> /, /about", "Low MOQ -> /about", "Sweatshop-free, made in USA -> /", "Garber System equipment -> /", "Customer service focus -> /about", "Organic Zone capabilities -> /about", "Full-service from concept to shipment -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "In La Apparel is a vertically integrated full package apparel and cut and sew manufacturers based in Los Angeles & Orange county, California United USA.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "5", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "Low MOQ", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='in-la-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Index Packaging, Inc. was founded in 1968 by Bill and Connie Lander in the basement of their New York home. The company moved to Milton, New Hampshire in 1981 and remains a closely held, family‑owned corporation now led by second‑generation shareholders including Bruce Lander, Debora Lussier, and Connie Lander. From its start as a small packaging operation, it has grown into a midsize manufacturer with four production and warehouse campuses across New Hampshire.

The company designs and manufactures custom packaging for fragile or high‑value items, producing foam inserts, corrugated boxes, wood crates and pallets, and specialty shippers such as apple gift boxes. All three material streams—foam, wood, and corrugated—are processed under one roof across facilities totaling more than 275,000 square feet. The operation employs over 200 people.

Index Packaging serves industrial equipment manufacturers, military and defense contractors, medical and pharmaceutical companies, laboratories, and food and agriculture businesses. Concrete examples include custom crates for sensitive instrumentation, foam‑filled shippers for fruit and produce, and protective packaging for cell‑phone and electronics shipments.

The business was built on a “Protection by Design” philosophy that emphasizes service, quality, and quick decision‑making enabled by its family ownership. An internal recycling program diverts polyurethane and polyethylene foam, corrugated scrap, and wood waste into secondary markets, and the company’s own logistics network allows it to guarantee on‑time delivery throughout New England.', certifications=ARRAY['ISPM-15']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom packaging design", "Engineering support", "Rapid prototyping", "Foam fabrication (polyurethane, polyethylene)", "Corrugated box manufacturing", "Wood crate and pallet manufacturing", "Kiln-drying (ISPM-15 compliance)", "Vendor managed inventory (VMI)", "Warehousing and just-in-time delivery", "Trucking and logistics (own fleet)", "Material sampling", "DIY prototyping kits", "Recycling of foam, corrugated, and wood waste"], "industries": ["Industrial equipment", "Military & defense", "Medical & pharmaceutical", "Laboratories", "Food & agriculture", "Technology"], "materials": ["Hardwood", "Softwood", "Corrugated fiberboard", "Polyurethane foam", "Polyethylene foam", "Expanded polystyrene (EPS)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["U.S.-based manufacturing in New Hampshire", "In-house design and engineering", "Foam, wood, and corrugated under one roof", "Nationwide shipping via LTL, FedEx, and UPS", "Own fleet for New England delivery"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1968 by Bill and Connie Lander in New York -> /about-us", "Headquarters moved to Milton, NH in 1981 -> /about-us", "Four NH facilities totaling 275,000+ sq ft across Milton, Dover, Merrimack, Somersworth -> /about-us", "Over 200 employees -> /about-us", "Family-owned, closely held corporation -> /about-us", "Products: wood crates, pallets, corrugated boxes, foam inserts, specialty shippers -> /", "Industries served: industrial, military, medical, food/agriculture -> /about-us", "ISPM-15 kiln-drying for export compliance -> /", "Services: VMI, warehousing, trucking, design/engineering/prototyping -> /services", "In-house design & engineering, foam/wood/corrugated under one roof -> /about-us", "Recycling program for foam, corrugated, wood waste -> /about-us", "Acquisitions: Timbertech, Kerrigan Paper, Plastifoam, Aegis Container, Avilite -> /about-us", "Own fleet for New England delivery -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Index Packaging''s manufacturing facility in Milton, New Hampshire specializes in wood packaging products, including wood crates and wood pallets, both new and recycled.", "founded_year": "1968", "employee_count": "200+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ISPM-15 compliant"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='index-packaging-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Industrial Fairway Supply has operated from Fargo, North Dakota for over 40 years, establishing itself as a distributor of industrial packaging supplies and equipment across the Midwest.

The firm stocks a broad line of packaging products including seals, pallets, rolled corrugate, steel and poly strapping, stretch wrap, foam bundles, corner protectors, lumber wrap, tape, and related tools. Beyond distribution, it offers custom packaging solutions and one-on-one consultations to assess customer needs, recommend materials, and improve packing efficiency. The company emphasizes same-day shipping on stocked items to minimize downtime for its clients.

Industrial Fairway Supply serves businesses throughout the United States and Canada that require industrial packaging materials and equipment.

