UPDATE companies SET description='Infant Ear Molding of New Hampshire, LLC operates from Fremont, New Hampshire. The clinic was founded by Dr. Emily Hurst, who holds a Doctor of Science degree from Massachusetts College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences and has a background in pediatric plastic surgery. Recognizing that many families lacked access to noninvasive ear correction, she established the practice as the first clinic in the state dedicated solely to infant ear molding.

The company provides a noninvasive, nonmedical ear molding service that uses a malleable splint to gently reshape an infant''s ear cartilage while it is still pliable, typically before the cartilage hardens around three months of age. The treatment process usually spans six weeks and is designed to correct prominent or misshapen ears without surgery or anesthesia.

The service is aimed at parents of newborns and infants with congenital auricular deformities.

Dr. Hurst''s specialization in pediatric plastic surgery and the clinic''s singular focus on ear molding differentiate it from general medical practices. The approach leverages a window of cartilage malleability to achieve lasting results, potentially sparing children from future psychosocial distress and surgical procedures.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Infant ear molding", "Noninvasive ear correction", "Ear splinting"], "industries": ["Pediatric healthcare", "Ear molding services", "Noninvasive cosmetic correction"], "materials": ["Malleable splint"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "6 weeks for typical treatment", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First dedicated infant ear molding clinic in New Hampshire", "Noninvasive, nonmedical ear correction using malleable splints", "Typical treatment completed in six weeks", "Founded by a pediatric plastic surgery specialist"], "facts_used": ["Company name, location, founder, service description -> /", "First dedicated clinic in New Hampshire -> /", "Treatment duration 6 weeks -> /", "Dr. Emily Hurst background -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Infant Ear Molding of New Hampshire, LLC offers professional ear molding service which can help correct the shape of your child''s ears. This noninvasive, nonmedical service involves using a malleable splint to hold the ear cartilage in the corrected shape until the cartilage hardens around 3 months of age.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='infant-ear-molding-of-new-hampshire-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Infineon Technologies Americas operates from Austin, Texas, as the U.S. arm of the global Infineon group founded in 1999. The company runs a design center in Texas and serves as a key node in Infineon’s worldwide network of 71 R&D sites and 15 manufacturing locations.

The company designs, develops, manufactures, and markets a broad portfolio of semiconductors, including power management ICs, microcontrollers, security ICs, silicon carbide MOSFET modules, IGBT modules, automotive MOSFETs, current sensors, stepper and servo motor drivers, 3D magnetic sensors, protection and monitoring ICs, and quasi-resonant switches. Beyond silicon, Infineon provides cloud services, engineering consulting, design-in support, and a developer center with software and tools for evaluation. Globally, the group employs over 58,000 people and generates approximately €15 billion in annual revenue.

Infineon’s customers span automotive, industrial, IoT, AI and communication, security, and consumer electronics sectors. Automotive OEMs use its MOSFETs and motor drivers for electric vehicles; industrial firms adopt current sensors and SiC modules for power infrastructure; consumer electronics makers integrate 3D sensors and security ICs. The company also supports a community of 160,000 engineers with 125,000 solutions and 1,700 code repositories.

