/", "Industries: Automotive, Industrial, AI & Communication, Security, Consumer -> /", "Developer community: 125K+ solutions, 160K+ engineers, 1700+ code repositories -> /", "Cloud services, engineering consulting, design-in support, developer center -> /services", "Purpose: green energy, clean mobility, smart secure IoT -> /about", "Website languages: English, Chinese, Japanese, German -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Infineon designs, develops, manufactures, and markets a broad range of solutions.", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "3000-9999", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["English", "Chinese", "Japanese", "German"], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='infineon-technologies-americas' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Infinity Molding & Assembly, Inc. was founded in 1982 in Mt. Vernon, Indiana, and operates two manufacturing facilities on a single campus in southwestern Indiana. The company is led by President & CEO Scott Titzer and Executive Vice President / CFO Sondra Ash.

The company specializes in custom plastic injection molding for difficult geometries and engineering-grade thermoplastics, including high-heat resins that require hot-oil mold temperature control. Its machine lineup spans 55 to 500 tons, supported by a separate 11,000-square-foot ISO Class 8 cleanroom for medical molding and white-room assembly. Automation cells employ Yushin, Staubli, Star Automation, Rethink Robotics, and Universal Robots equipment, and electronic vision systems handle in-process inspection. Secondary assembly operations round out the offering.

Infinity serves the medical device, automotive, consumer goods, and industrial sectors. Medical device companies of all sizes rely on its ISO 13485-certified cleanroom, while automotive customers are supported through IATF 16949 compliance. The firm also produces components for consumer and industrial applications.

Management emphasizes that the cleanroom is the only one of its kind within a 300-mile radius, and that a workforce capable of both individual and team performance drives quality. The company highlights its "Made in America" positioning as a differentiator for delivery and quality, backed by ISO 9001, ISO 13485, ISO 14001, and IATF 16949 certifications.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','ISO 14001','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "High tolerance injection molding", "Cleanroom medical molding (ISO Class 8)", "Automotive parts manufacturing", "Secondary assembly operations", "Hot oil mold temperature control", "Engineering grade thermoplastics processing", "High heat resins processing", "Electronic vision inspection", "Robotics automation", "White room assembly"], "industries": ["Medical device", "Automotive", "Consumer goods", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Engineering grade thermoplastics", "High heat resins"], "equipment": ["Yushin robots", "Staubli robots", "Star Automation equipment", "Rethink Robotics equipment", "Universal Robots equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only ISO Class 8 cleanroom within a 300-mile radius", "Machine range of 55 to 500 tons for diverse part sizes", "Advanced robotics from Yushin, Staubli, Star Automation, Rethink Robotics, and Universal Robots", "Electronic vision inspection for quality assurance", "ISO 9001, ISO 13485, ISO 14001, and IATF 16949 certifications"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 -> db, /", "Headquarters Mt Vernon, Indiana -> db, /", "Certifications ISO 9001, ISO 13485, ISO 14001, IATF 16949 -> db, /", "Custom plastic injection molding, difficult geometries, engineering grade thermoplastics, high heat resins, hot oil systems -> /", "Machine sizes 55 to 500 tons -> /", "Two facilities: Automotive/Industrial and Medical/Healthcare -> /", "11,000 sq ft ISO Class 8 cleanroom -> /", "Automation: Yushin, Staubli, Star Automation, Rethink Robotics, Universal Robots -> /", "Electronic vision and inspection systems -> /", "Industries: medical device, automotive, consumer goods, industrial -> /", "President & CEO Scott Titzer, Executive Vice President / CFO Sondra Ash -> /", "Cleanroom only one of its kind within 300-mile radius -> /", "Made in America emphasis -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Infinity Molding & Assembly, Inc. is a custom plastic injection molder specializing in difficult geometries and engineering grade thermoplastics incorporating high heat resins requiring hot oil systems for mold temperature control.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/infinity-plastics-group/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='infinity-molding-assembly' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Nashville, Tennessee, Inline Electric Supply Co. operates as a regional electrical distributor with a network spanning four southeastern states. The company, formerly known as Williams Electric Supply Co., maintains its headquarters in Nashville and serves customers through more than 25 branch locations across Alabama, Florida, Georgia, and Tennessee.

The company distributes a broad range of electrical products and equipment for construction, repair, and maintenance projects. Its inventory includes panelboards up to 1,200 amps and switchboards up to 4,000 amps, sourced through partnerships with Eaton and Siemens. Inline also operates lighting showrooms and provides lighting design consultations performed by certified professionals, alongside energy consultation services for commercial and industrial facilities.

Inline serves a mix of public and private institutions, government contractors, commercial and industrial businesses, and residential customers.

