UPDATE companies SET description='Innovative Injection Tech (i2-tech) was founded in 1960 in West Des Moines, Iowa, initially producing fishing lures for the Lazy Ike company.

Today the company specializes in large-part injection molding, operating 11 presses over 1,000 tons of clamping force, including a 4,400-ton Engel press installed in 2021 capable of molding parts up to 45 pounds. The facility runs 24/7 with a workforce of over 200 employees and focuses on low- to medium-volume production of highly engineered plastic components and sub-assemblies. Mold tooling is built in Shenzhen, China, to U.S. standards using German steel, with final qualification performed in Iowa.

The company serves original equipment manufacturers in agriculture, industrial equipment, automotive (including Tier 1 suppliers), construction, medical devices, and recreational vehicles. Typical parts include ATV bumpers, personal watercraft hoods, UTV fenders, and other large cosmetic assemblies.

i2-tech emphasizes a culture built on trust, respect, and camaraderie across customers, employees, suppliers, shareholders, and the community. It cites its technical expertise, financial stability, and round-the-clock operations as key differentiators, along with in-house engineering, scientific molding processes, and advanced measurement technology such as a portable Romer CMM with integrated scanner.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 2001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Large press injection molding (55\u20134,400 tons)", "Contract molding", "Mold trials and qualification", "Mold transfer programs", "Low-cost mold building and tooling (offshore with U.S. oversight)", "Scientific injection molding", "Degating fixture design and build", "Rapid prototyping (Stratasys 3D printing)", "Color analysis", "Moisture analysis", "Melt flow analysis", "Design of experiments (DOE) studies", "Assembly and sub-assembly", "Contract manufacturing (turnkey)"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Industrial equipment", "Automotive (Tier 1)", "Construction", "Medical devices", "Recreational vehicles"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Engel 4,400-ton injection molding machine (654 oz barrel)", "Stratasys 3D printer", "Romer Portable CMM with Integrated Scanner", "Electric and servo-hydraulic injection molding presses (55\u20134,400 tons)", "Robotic automation on all presses"], "volume": "Low to medium lot sizes", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24/7 operation with over 200 employees", "11 large-tonnage presses up to 4,400 tons", "Mold tooling built in China to U.S. standards with final approval in Iowa", "Scientific molding and advanced CMM inspection for repeatable quality", "Proven mold transfer capability (200+ molds transferred in 2020)"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1960 making fishing lures for Lazy Ike -> db", "Headquarters in West Des Moines, Iowa -> db", "Over 200 employees, 24/7 operation -> /about", "11 presses over 1000 tons, largest 4400-ton Engel press in