UPDATE companies SET description='Innovative Plastek Solutions was founded in 2012 in the Shoals region of northern Alabama, initially as a urethane molder producing decorative furniture components.

The shop specializes in thermoplastic injection molding with presses up to 270 tons, 21.2‑ounce shot capacity, and 32‑inch maximum part length, complemented by urethane casting for low‑to‑medium volumes. In‑house capabilities include overmolding, insert molding, secondary machining, a range of coatings and vacuum metalizing, value‑added assembly and kitting, 3D‑printed prototyping, and a conversion service that moves parts from urethane to injection‑molded production. A finished‑goods warehouse supports just‑in‑time delivery, and the company maintains a fleet of box trucks and vans for freight.

Primary markets include the furniture industry (promotional hardware, decorative trim), automotive (child‑seat components, interior parts), consumer products, and military/defense (precision molded parts). The company also serves aerospace and healthcare sectors, and ships throughout North America.

The founders aimed to undercut larger northern molders by converting urethane designs to injection‑molded parts, lowering per‑unit cost while maintaining quick turnaround. Leadership cites over 60 years of combined molding experience, a full‑service model from design through logistics, and a focus on quality, price, and service as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thermoplastic injection molding (up to 270 ton, 21.2 oz shot, 32 in)", "Urethane casting", "Overmolding", "Insert molding", "Secondary machining and finishing", "Coatings and vacuum metalizing", "Value-added assembly and kitting", "3D printed prototyping", "Short-run production", "Urethane-to-injection-mold conversion", "Freight and logistics (fleet of box trucks and vans)", "JIT warehousing", "Customer tooling storage", "Mold maintenance", "Design and engineering support", "Turnkey solutions", "Quality assurance"], "industries": ["Furniture", "Automotive", "Consumer Products", "Military/Defense", "Aerospace", "Healthcare", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines (up to 270 ton, 21.2 oz shot, 32 in clamp)", "3D printers for sampling", "Box trucks and vans for freight", "Vacuum metalizing system", "Coating and finishing equipment"], "volume": "Low to medium volumes; short runs to medium series", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Converts urethane prototypes to injection\u2011molded production for lower unit cost", "In\u2011house freight fleet (box trucks and vans) for direct delivery", "JIT warehousing and customer tooling storage", "3D\u2011printed samples for short\u2011run validation", "Over 60 years of combined molding experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2012 -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Loretto, Tennessee -> db and /", "Originally urethane molder for decorative furniture parts -> /about-us", "Thermoplastic injection molding up to 270 ton, 21.2 oz shot, 32 in length -> / and /services", "Urethane c