UPDATE companies SET description='International Crankshaft Inc. (ICI) operates from Georgetown, Kentucky, where it was founded in 1992 as a single-line forge shop. The company is now part of the Nippon Steel Corporation Group, the world''s largest steel group by market capitalization. Since its founding, ICI has consistently grown from a one-line forge shop to a four-line operation.

ICI specializes in crankshaft forging and has expanded to four high-speed production lines. Its equipment includes a 5,000-ton high-speed press installed in 2015 from Sumitomo Heavy Industries. In 2015 the company forged more than three million crankshafts for American cars and light trucks. The shift from casting to forging technology underscores its process expertise.

The company serves the North American automotive sector, supplying crankshafts for passenger cars and light trucks.

