UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1972 in Norwood, Massachusetts, Intronics Power Inc. (operating as Intronics Inc) began as a designer and manufacturer of high-reliability power conversion and signal processing solutions. The company maintains a facility in Longmont, Colorado, and holds CAGE code 30635 for government contracting.

Intronics produces a broad line of DC/DC converters—including isolated and non-isolated modules up to 1 kW—alongside precision signal amplifiers and high-speed image processors. Its engineering services span analog and digital circuit design, embedded hardware and software development, and full validation testing. The firm also provides contract manufacturing for printed circuit board and electromechanical assemblies, with a catalog of hundreds of standard model numbers such as the 277, 289, and SHA1144 series.

The company serves aerospace and defense, medical device, electric power utility, transportation, industrial automation, computers and communications, space systems, and emerging technology sectors such as AI hardware and quantum computing. Customers include satellite engineers, medical imaging R&D directors, and automotive plant managers who rely on Intronics components for mission-critical systems.

Intronics emphasizes its ISO 9001:2015 certified manufacturing, MIL-STD compliant design practices for defense programs, and radiation-hardened electronics qualified for space vehicles. Testimonials highlight the reliability of its converters in extreme environments, the expertise of its engineering team in custom signal conditioning, and a track record of zero failures in harsh industrial settings.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Analog circuit design", "Digital / microprocessor circuit design", "Embedded systems hardware and software development", "Electronics testing and troubleshooting", "Component level electronic evaluation", "Electronics functional testing and verification & validation", "Printed circuit board (PCB) assembly", "Electromechanical device assembly", "DC/DC converter design and manufacturing", "Signal amplifier design and manufacturing", "Image processor design and manufacturing"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Medical Device", "Electric Power Utility", "Transportation", "Industrial Automation", "Computers & Communication", "Space Systems", "Emerging Technologies (AI hardware, quantum computing)"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified manufacturing facilities", "MIL-STD compliant designs for defense applications", "Radiation-hardened electronics for space and satellite programs", "Custom engineering services covering analog, digital, and embedded design", "Contract manufacturing for PCB and electromechanical assemblies"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1972 -> db", "Headquarters in Norwood, Massachusetts -> db", "CAGE code 30635 -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified manufacturing -> /", "MIL-STD compliant designs for defense -> /", "Products: DC/DC converters, signal amplifiers, image processors -> /", "Engineering services: analog/digital/embedded design, testing, validation -> /", "Contract manufacturing: PCB assemblie