UPDATE companies SET description='J G Plastics Group LLC operates from Costa Mesa, California, adjacent to John Wayne Airport in Orange County. The company was founded in 1975 and has since provided total plastic solutions for medical, aerospace, consumer, defense, and electronic/connector industries.

The facility functions as a complete plastic injection molding operation, running both thermoplastic and thermoset processes. An in-house mold making department uses CAD/CAM software to build complex tooling, while secondary operations include assembly, in-mold decoration, insert molding, overmolding, medical mesh overmolding, painting, shielding, and packaging.

Customers span medical device manufacturers, aerospace and defense contractors requiring FAA and MIL-SPEC compliance, electronic and connector producers, and consumer product brands. The company molds parts from materials such as TPE/TPU/TPV elastomers, conductive and shielding plastics, high-strength resins, medical-grade polymers, PPS, LCP, and Elvax (EVA) copolymers. Finished components ship throughout the United States, Canada, Mexico, Europe, and Asia.

J G Plastics emphasizes scientific molding principles and decades of mold-making experience to achieve close-tolerance results that, in its words, accomplish what others cannot. Registration to ISO 9001:2015, AS9100D, and ISO 13485:2016, along with ITAR registration, underpins a quality system aligned with Good Manufacturing Practices for regulated sectors.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D','ISO 13485:2016','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding (thermoplastic)", "Thermoset molding", "Mold making (in-house, CAD/CAM)", "Assembly / secondary operations", "Medical device assembly", "Close tolerance molding", "In-mold decoration", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Medical mesh overmolding", "Class 10,000 cleanroom molding (ISO 7)", "Class 10,000 cleanroom assembly (ISO 7)", "Painting", "Shielding", "Packaging"], "industries": ["Medical", "Aerospace", "Defense / Military / Tactical", "Electronic / Connector", "Consumer"], "materials": ["TPE/TPU/TPV Elastomers", "Conductive & Shielding Plastics", "High Strength Plastics", "Medical Grade Plastics", "PPS and LCP Plastics", "Elvax (EVA) Copolymer Resins"], "equipment": ["Horizontal injection molding machines", "Vertical injection molding machines", "Class 10,000/ISO 7 cleanrooms"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house mold making with CAD/CAM tooling design", "Dedicated Class 10,000/ISO 7 cleanrooms for medical molding and assembly", "Scientific molding principles for close-tolerance parts", "ITAR registered and compliant with FAA/MIL-SPEC requirements", "Global shipping to US, Canada, Mexico, Europe, Asia"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1975 -> db", "Headquarters Costa Mesa, California -> db, /", "ISO 9001:2015, AS9100D, ISO 13485:2016, ITAR certifications -> /", "Plastic injection molding (thermoplastic & thermoset) -> /, /about-us, /capabilities", "Mold making in-house with CAD/CAM -> /, /capabilities", "Assembly/secondary operations including medical device assembly -> /, /capabilities", "Specialties: close tolerance molding, in-mold decoration, insert molding, overmolding, medical mesh overmolding -> /, /capabilities", "Class 10,000/ISO 7 cleanroom molding and assembly (2,000 sq ft) -> /", "Horizontal and vertical injection molding machines -> /", "Industries served: Medical, Aerospace, Defense/Military/Tactical, Electronic/Connector, Consumer -> /, /capabilities", "Materials: TPE/TPU/TPV, Conductive & Shielding, High Strength, Medical Grade, PPS/LCP, Elvax (EVA) -> /, /capabilities", "Scientific molding principles, GMP, FAA/MIL SPEC compliance -> /", "Location adjacent to John Wayne Airport, shipping to US, Canada, Mexico, Europe, Asia -> /", "Painting, shielding, packaging services -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a complete plastic injection molding facility including thermoplastic and thermoset molding", "founded_year": "1975", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered", "Export to Canada, Mexico, Europe, Asia"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-g-plastics-group-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J. Alexander Fine Woodworking operates from Nampa, Idaho, in the Treasure Valley. Jared Patchin began building furniture in 1991 after his father acquired Shutter Crafts, a local wood shutter company. Patchin later studied production management at Boise State University and has led J. Alexander for 17 years.

The shop produces custom residential cabinetry and fine furniture. Every project is rendered in a 3D environment to verify specifications, then translated into digital drawings for precise CNC machining and hand-finishing. The team combines computerized cutting with traditional building methods, adapting techniques as they evolve.

The company distinguishes itself by rendering every product in 3D before production, ensuring dimensional accuracy, and by blending CNC precision with hand craftsmanship. Patchin''s original motivation—building furniture from scrap wood—still drives a culture of continuous learning and method refinement.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["3D rendering", "CAD/digital drawings", "CNC machining", "Hand woodworking", "Custom cabinetry fabrication", "Fine furniture making"], "industries": ["Residential cabinetry", "Fine woodworking"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CNC machine"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["3D rendering of all products for specification accuracy", "State-of-the-art design software with digital drawings and CNC cut-outs", "Combination of CNC machining and hand craftsmanship", "Continuous innovation in building methods"], "facts_used": ["Company located in Nampa, Idaho -> db", "Jared Patchin began building furniture in 1991 after father bought Shutter Crafts -> /", "Patchin studied civil engineering then production management at Boise State University -> /", "Patchin has run J. Alexander for 17 years -> /", "Company renders all products in 3D environment for accurate specifications -> /about-us", "Uses state-of-the-art design software, digital drawings, CNC machine, and hand work -> /about-us", "Employs seasoned professionals who implement best building methods and continuously innovate -> /about-us", "Specializes in residential cabinetry -> /", "Address: 3122 Port Street, Nampa, ID -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Jared Patchin started building furniture in 1991 when his father bought Shutter Crafts.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-alexander-fine-woodworking' AND approved AND p