UPDATE companies SET description='J.Q. Dickinson Salt-Works operates from Charleston, West Virginia, where siblings Nancy Bruns and Lewis Payne revived their family''s salt-making legacy in 2013. The Dickinson family had been among the region''s largest producers for more than 120 years, during a period when the area led the country in salt output with over 50 businesses and 100 wells. The current incarnation draws on that heritage, positioning itself as an artisan salt company rooted in Appalachian tradition.

The company harvests brine from an ancient ocean deposit sealed beneath the Appalachian Mountains, then slow-sun-dries it in small batches to produce a mineral-rich finishing salt with a distinctive texture. Its product line includes plain heirloom finishing salt, cooking and popcorn salt, grinding salt, and a range of flavored blends such as mushroom herb, bourbon-barrel smoked, bloody mary, and ghost pepper. Beyond salt, the mercantile curates spice blend gift sets, sampler boxes, and other handcrafted pantry and home goods from regional artisans.

Customers include home chefs, gift buyers, and wholesale accounts; the company explicitly invites retailers to carry its products and lists a Faire storefront for trade orders. Its subscription boxes and gift sets target the specialty food and gifting markets, while the salt guide and educational content serve culinary enthusiasts seeking authenticity.

The founders emphasize family heritage, sustainability, and traditional methods as differentiators, stating that every item reflects a commitment to quality and authenticity. By working with artisans who share their values, they aim to keep the spirit of Appalachia alive in each jar and bag.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hand harvesting", "Solar evaporation (slow sun drying)", "Small-batch production", "Salt blending and flavoring", "Gift set curation", "Wholesale distribution", "Subscription box fulfillment"], "industries": ["Specialty food", "Gourmet food", "Gift and specialty retail", "Wholesale", "E-commerce"], "materials": ["Appalachian brine", "Sea salt", "Applewood smoke", "Bourbon barrels", "Ramps", "Mushrooms", "Herbs", "Ghost peppers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Location: Charleston, West Virginia -> db", "Revival year: 2013 by Nancy Bruns and Lewis Payne -> db", "Historical family production >120 years, region leading producer -> db", "Hand-harvested from ancient ocean brine under Appalachian Mountains -> /", "Slow-sun-dried, small-batch methods -> /", "Product varieties: heirloom finishing, cooking/popcorn, grinding, flavored blends -> /", "Curated gift sets, sampler boxes, subscription boxes -> /", "Wholesale invitation and Faire storefront -> /", "Commitment to family heritage, sustainability, traditional methods -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As an artisan salt company, we rely on small-batch methods to retain the true essence of natural sea salt.", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-q-dickinson-salt-works' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='JAMM Fabrication & Design was founded in 2017 in North Little Rock, Arkansas, by co-owners Matt Goodhart and Allen Walker. The business began when Walker, a welder since high school, recognized a need for custom handrails for train cars and taught himself to fabricate them. The initial three-person team produced hundreds of handrails, laying the groundwork for a shop that now serves customers across the United States.

The 24-person team ships roughly 50,000 custom parts per month from a facility expanded in spring 2025, with a Texas location planned.

JAMM serves three primary segments: architecture and construction (structural components, railings, bridge parts), manufacturing and industrial (conveyor components, high-volume production parts), and custom specialty jobs (sculptures, fixtures, signage for individuals and businesses).

