 -> /services", "Equipment specs: laser bed 60.25x120.25, press brake 220-ton 10ft, pipe bender 5-axis 3.5 OD, plate roller 18ga-3/8, powder oven 8x8x30, 7 CNC lathes/mills -> /services", "Industries: Architecture & Construction, Manufacturing & Industrial, Custom & Specialty Jobs -> /", "Mission statement -> /about", "Free quotes -> /", "Expanded to new North Little Rock facility spring 2025, Texas planned -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a custom shop capable of providing production-level work.", "founded_year": "2017", "employee_count": "24", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='jamm-fabrication-design' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='JATCO Incorporated, a custom plastic injection molding company, was founded in 1976 in Union City, California, in the San Francisco Bay Area. The company later relocated to a larger facility in Modesto, California, where it operates today.

The company provides custom plastic injection molding services including overmolding, as well as die casting, metal stamping, product design, engineering, tooling, assembly, painting, packaging, warehousing, and distribution. JATCO also manufactures and sells its own product lines: concrete cylinder molds under the TestCylinderMolds brand and seedling trays under the Plantway brand. The Modesto plant operates 24 hours a day, seven days a week, and the company notes operations on two continents.

