UPDATE companies SET description='JEM Electronics, Inc. was founded in 1981 in Franklin, Massachusetts, by John McDonald, who remains president and CEO. After years in the wire and cable industry, McDonald saw that custom cable and harness assemblies were still being built with traditional methods.

Today JEM operates as a contract manufacturer specializing in custom cable assemblies, wire harnesses, and electromechanical box-build assemblies. The company runs ISO 9001:2015–certified facilities in Franklin, MA, and Tijuana, Mexico, providing both domestic and near-shore capacity. Every build follows a documented process: drawings are reviewed for manufacturability before quoting, assemblies meet IPC/WHMA-A-620 and IPC-J-STD-001 standards, and 100% of units undergo in-house testing—including continuity, hipot, VSWR, and pull testing—before shipment. Volume ranges from prototype to high-volume production.

JEM serves OEMs in regulated, high-reliability sectors including military and defense (ITAR-registered, CAGE 3DTF7), medical and healthcare, semiconductor equipment, robotics, renewable energy, oil and gas, and networking. The company emphasizes full traceability and on-schedule delivery for applications where cable failure is not an option.

Leadership cites a culture of cross-trained assemblers and Lean Six Sigma continuous improvement that enables flexible staffing and waste reduction. JEM promises transparent quoting grounded in actual component lead times, a manufacturability review that catches terminal or routing issues early, and a commitment to “get builds right the first time, document every step, and stand behind every assembly we ship.”', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IPC/WHMA-A-620','ITAR','IPC-J-STD-001','UL/CSA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assembly manufacturing", "Wire harness assembly", "Electromechanical assembly", "Box-build assembly", "Continuity and resistance testing", "VSWR testing", "Hipot testing", "Pull testing", "Build-to-print services", "Rapid prototyping", "Scalable production", "Lean Six Sigma process improvement", "Statistical process control (SPC)", "Cross-trained assembler program", "Manufacturability design review", "Supply chain management"], "industries": ["Military & Defense", "Medical & Healthcare", "Semiconductor", "Robotics", "Renewable Energy", "Oil & Gas", "Networking"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "Quoted schedule adherence; transparent timelines based on actual build complexity", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% in-house testing (continuity, hipot, VSWR, pull)", "Manufacturability review before quoting", "Transparent quoting with actual lead times", "ITAR registered with CAGE 3DTF7", "Dual-site production in Franklin, MA and Tijuana, MX"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1981 by John McDonald -> /about-us", "Headquarters Franklin, MA -> /about-us", "Facilities in Franklin, MA and Tijuana, MX -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "IPC/WHMA-A-620 certified -> /quality", "ITAR registered -> /", "CAGE 3DTF7 -> /", "Custom cable assembly, wire harness, electromechanical assembly capabilities -> /", "Industries served: Military & Defense, Medical, Semicondu