UPDATE companies SET description='Jones Plastic & Engineering was founded in 1961 in Louisville, Kentucky, by brothers Harry and Larry Jones as a single-machine operation producing whiskey bottle caps. The family-owned business, now headed by the second and third generations of the Jones family, is based in Jeffersontown, Kentucky, and operates nine facilities across the United States and Mexico.

The company provides integrated plastic manufacturing services, spanning product development, tooling, injection molding (65 to 3,150 tons across five facilities), robotic painting and hydrographics, assembly, and testing. A 90,000-square-foot paint and hydrographics plant in Juárez, Mexico, includes a 25,000-square-foot clean-room line with FANUC robots and a 1.3-meter dip tank. An in-house 3D printing lab runs FDM and PolyJet systems for functional prototypes and short-run molded samples. Total manufacturing space approaches 1.6 million square feet, supported by roughly 3,000 employees. The firm also owns Rev-A-Shelf, a subsidiary producing residential cabinet storage products.

Jones Plastic serves automotive, appliance, powersports, outdoor products, consumer goods, and industrial and defense markets, supplying North American OEMs with components and assemblies that require Class-A cosmetic finishes and tight tolerances.

The company pioneered gas-assist injection molding in the early 1990s and emphasizes an engineering-first approach, using Moldex3D mold-flow analysis and finite element analysis to validate designs before tooling. Integrating molding, finishing, and assembly under one supply chain aims to reduce freight, handling, and coordination costs for near-shore production. Quality management is ISO 9001 certified.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding (65\u20133,150 tons)", "Gas-assist injection molding (GAIM)", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Robotic assembly", "In-mold labeling", "Prototyping (FDM, PolyJet 3D printing)", "Tooling design, construction, and PPAP management", "Mold maintenance and engineering changes", "Robotic painting (clean-room)", "Hydrographics (dip up to 1.3 m)", "Assembly and testing (pressure decay leak testing, destructive testing, dimensional inspection)", "Decoration (hot stamping, pad printing, heat transfer labeling, laser etching)", "Product development (solid modeling, CAE simulation, industrial design)", "Finite element analysis (FEA)", "Mold filling analysis (Moldex3D)", "Stack molding", "Family and MUD base tooling", "Robotic adhesive dispensing", "Digital torque verification", "Warehousing and logistics", "Material selection guidance"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Appliance", "Powersports", "Outdoor products", "Consumer goods", "Industrial and defense"], "materials": ["Commodity thermoplastics", "Engineering-grade thermoplastics"], "equipment": ["FANUC robots", "RFID-controlled rack systems", "1.3-meter hydrographic dip tank", "FDM 3D printers", "PolyJet 3D printers", "Clean-room paint line"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Pioneered gas-assist injection molding in the early 1990s", "90,000 sq ft robotic paint and hydrographics facility with 1.3-meter dip tank", "In-house 3D printing lab for functional prototypes and short-run molded samples", "Global tooling network with in-house mold maintenance and engineering change capability", "Integrated molding, finishing, and assembly under a single supply chain"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1961 in Louisville, Kentucky by Harry and Larry Jones -> /about", "Family-owned, second and third generations active -> /about", "Approximately 3,000 employees across 1.6 million sq ft -> /about", "Nine facilities in US and Mexico -> /about", "Rev-A-Shelf subsidiary -> /about", "Injection molding 65-3,150 tons across five facilities -> /", "90,000 sq ft paint and hydrographics facility in Juarez with 25,000 sq ft clean room -> /", "FANUC robots, RFID-controlled rack systems, 1.3-meter hydrographic dip tank -> /", "In-house 3D printing lab with FDM and PolyJet -> /", "Industries: automotive, appliance, powersports, outdoor products, consumer goods, industrial and defense -> /", "ISO 9001 certified -> /about", "Gas-assist injection molding pioneered early 1990s -> /about", "Engineering-first approach with Moldex3D and FEA -> /services", "Global tooling network with in-house mold maintenance -> /services", "Stack molds, family tools, MUD base molds -> /services", "Robotic assembly, adhesive dispensing, digital torque guns -> /services", "Pressure decay leak testing, destructive testing, dimensional checks -> /services", "Decoration: in-mold labeling, hot stamping, pad printing, heat transfer labeling, laser etching -> /services", "Headquarters Jeffersontown, Kentucky -> db", "Certifications ISO9001 -> db", "Capabilities from db: Value Added Services, Injection Molding, Prototyping Services -> db", "Industries served from db: Industrial and Defense -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom injection molding from 65 to 3,150 tons across five injection facilities", "founded_year": "1961", "employee_count": "approximately 3,000", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Fami