UPDATE companies SET description='K & F Electronics was founded in 1972 in Fraser, Michigan, a suburb of Detroit. The company remains a third-generation family-owned business, with the founder''s grandchildren now overseeing operations. From a single facility, the firm has grown into a full-service provider of printed circuit board fabrication, assembly, and design.

The company produces single-sided, double-sided, and multilayer rigid boards, as well as flex and rigid-flex circuits with blind and buried vias. Materials include FR-4, Rogers, Taconic, Arlon, Nelco, Teflon, polyimide, and aluminum. Assembly services cover surface-mount, through-hole, and box-build work, supported by automated SMT lines rated at 18,000–30,000 components per hour, selective soldering, and hand soldering for special requirements. In-house engineering handles schematic design, PCB layout, bill-of-materials generation, and reverse engineering of existing boards. Additional services include 3D printing of prototypes, wire stripping, conformal coating (acrylic), flying-probe electrical testing, and PCB drilling and routing. All boards pass through a multi-level inspection process that includes AOI, X-ray, and dimensional checks to IPC Class 3.

K & F Electronics serves customers needing quick-turn prototypes and production quantities, offering expedited lead times from 24 hours to four weeks. The firm can begin assembly the same day the final component arrives.

The company emphasizes its integrated design-through-assembly model, a return rate below 1 percent, and a one-year warranty on all PCBs and PCBAs. ITAR registration since 2009 and ISO 9001:2015 certification support work with defense and regulated customers. The family legacy and same-day assembly capability are cited as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR','IPC-6012 Class 1-3','RoHS','UL Approved #E71379']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Single-sided PCB fabrication", "Double-sided PCB fabrication", "Multilayer PCB fabrication", "Flex circuit fabrication", "Rigid-flex circuit fabrication", "Blind and buried via fabrication", "Surface mount technology (SMT) assembly", "Through-hole assembly", "Box build assembly", "PCB design and layout", "Reverse engineering", "3D printing of prototypes", "Wire stripping", "Conformal coating (acrylic)", "Flying probe electrical testing", "PCB drilling and routing", "Gerber file creation", "PCB scanning from films, prints, and bare boards", "Design rule check", "Component substitution engineering"], "industries": [], "materials": ["FR-4", "Rogers", "Taconic", "Arlon", "Nelco", "Ro4350B", "Teflon", "Polyimide", "Aluminum", "Flex circuit materials"], "equipment": ["VJ Electronix XQuik II X-Ray parts counter", "Techspray Turbo-Coat conformal coating system", "Fancort Industries VPD3-1S scoring machine", "Fancort Industries VPD3-1S de-paneler"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day assembly after last component arrives; expedited options from 24 hours to 4 weeks", "tolerances": "Dimensional tolerances up to IPC Class 3; coating tolerances \u00b15 \u00b5m (non-electro) and \u00b110 \u00b5m (electro)", "built_on": ["One-year warranty on all PCBs and PCBAs", "Return rate below 1%", "ITAR registered since 2009", "Same-day assembly after last component arrives", "Expedited lead times from 24 hours to four weeks"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 -> /about", "Headquarters Fraser, Michigan -> /about", "Third-gen