UPDATE companies SET description='KOA Speer Electronics Inc operates from Bradford, Pennsylvania, where it develops and manufactures a range of passive electronic components. The company positions itself as a passive component partner for designers seeking resistors with specialized performance characteristics.

Its product portfolio centers on resistor technologies built for demanding environments. Current sense resistors use a metal plate structure to handle large current detection across multiple sizes, power ratings, and resistance values. The SG73 series of thick film resistors addresses surge and pulse voltage protection, while thin film lines such as RN73R, RN73H, and the wide terminal WN73H deliver high precision for automotive and industrial circuits. Wide terminal chip resistors employ a reverse geometry that improves heat dissipation and enables higher power ratings in the same footprint. Anti-sulfur variants incorporate a sulfuration-proof inner electrode and metal glaze thick film, qualified to AEC-Q200 and ASTM-B809 standards.

The company serves primarily the automotive and industrial electronics sectors, supplying components that meet automotive reliability requirements such as AEC-Q200. Its resistors are designed into power supply protection, circuit control, and high-reliability applications where sulfuration resistance and pulse withstand capability are critical.

KOA Speer differentiates itself through its metal plate current sense technology, wide terminal architecture for thermal performance, and a focus on anti-sulfur solutions that address silver electrode degradation in harsh environments. The firm also emphasizes sample availability for design validation.', certifications=ARRAY['AEC-Q200','ASTM-B809']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Current sense resistor manufacturing", "Surge/pulse withstanding resistor manufacturing (SG73 series)", "Thin film resistor manufacturing (RN73R, RN73H, WN73H)", "Wide terminal resistor manufacturing", "Anti-sulfur resistor manufacturing", "Metal plate technology", "Thick film resistor manufacturing", "AEC-Q200 qualification", "ASTM-B809 anti-sulfuration testing"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Metal plate technology for large current detection", "Wide terminal reverse geometry for higher power density", "Anti-sulfur resistors qualified to AEC-Q200 and ASTM-B809", "Surge and pulse withstanding thick film resistors (SG73 series)", "Thin film high precision resistors for automotive and industrial use"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Bradford, Pennsylvania -> db", "Manufactures current sense resistors with metal plate technology -> /", "Offers surge and pulse withstanding voltage resistors (SG73 series) -> /", "Produces thin film high precision resistors (RN73R, RN73H, WN73H) -> /", "Provides wide terminal resistors for higher power ratings -> /", "Supplies anti-sulfur resistors tested to AEC-Q200 and ASTM-B809 -> /", "Serves automotive and industrial markets -> /", "AEC-Q200 qualification -> /", "ASTM-B809 anti-sulfuration testing -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "KOA Speer''s family of current sense resistors offer excellent large current detection due to its metal plate technology.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "