UPDATE companies SET description='Kato Cable was founded in 2006 in Mankato, Minnesota, with a vision to create a different kind of wire harness and cable assembly company focused on employee success and innovation. The company operates from a 12-acre campus with 63,000 square feet of manufacturing space Leadership includes Chairman & CEO Eric Else and President Matt Lade.

The company manufactures wire harnesses, cable assemblies, electro-mechanical assemblies, and battery cables. Its in-house capabilities span wire marking, processing, automation, ultrasonic welding, braiding, and overmolding, supported by process control and engineering control services. Equipment includes a Komax Zeta high-performance wire processing system for measuring, marking, cutting, stripping, and crimping.

Kato Cable serves OEMs and distributors across power generation, commercial vehicle, powersports, medical, industrial, and agriculture markets.

