UPDATE companies SET description='Keach & Company Woodworking operates from Chester, Virginia, where owner and woodworker Karl Keach has been building custom projects since 2018. Keach learned the craft from his father, a high school shop teacher, and began taking on commissions for family, friends, and customers while living in the Richmond area. The business serves the eastern half of Virginia in person and ships nationwide through its website and Etsy shop.

The shop specializes in custom woodworking and laser engraving, producing items such as challenge coin displays (in 12-, 26-, and 50-coin configurations), commemorative plaques, serving trays, charcuterie boards, furniture, and clocks. The operation is a one-person workshop; no facility size or headcount beyond the owner is disclosed.

Customers include law enforcement agencies, military units, National Park Service personnel, first responders, veterans, and private collectors. Concrete examples from the product line include a National Park Service Buffalo Badge plaque, a Chief Ranger plaque, and a Chesterfield County Police badge engraving. The shop also creates retirement awards and recognition plaques for government and organizational clients.

