UPDATE companies SET description='Kelley Bean Co. traces its roots to 1927 when the Chester B. Brown Company was founded in Morrill, Nebraska, with Robert L. Kelley Sr. as plant manager. The business evolved through family leadership: Kelley became president in 1941, then left in 1969 to establish Kelley Bean Co. in Henry, Nebraska, alongside his son Gary. The two entities merged in 1982 under Gary''s leadership, and today the company is an employee- and family-owned enterprise headquartered in Scottsbluff, Nebraska, now guided by a fourth generation led by Kevin Kelley.

The company processes and markets dry edible beans — including Pinto, Great Northern, and other varieties — sourced directly from a network of grower partners. Its facilities run a multi-step cleaning line known as ''triple clean'': beans pass over round and slot-hole screens for size separation, gravity tables and de-stoners for weight separation, and optical electric-eye sorters that eject off-color or damaged beans by air puff. Additional equipment includes rare-earth magnets, metal detectors, and prewash systems. All plants operate under the internally developed P.A.S.S. System, a GFSI-aligned food safety program, and multiple sites hold GFSI certification and pass annual AIB audits.

Kelley Bean serves food manufacturers, canners, food-service distributors, and retail packers across the U.S. and internationally (notably a 2006 export sale to Cuba).

The firm cites its employee stock ownership plan (launched in 1983), multi-generational family stewardship, and a culture of ''absolute integrity, hard work, dedication, service, and community involvement'' as differentiators. The P.A.S.S. System and direct grower traceability are presented as unique safeguards for quality and safety from field to bag.', certifications=ARRAY['GFSI certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Dry bean cleaning (triple clean)", "Milling and sizing", "Gravity separation and de-stoning", "Optical sorting (electric eye sorter)", "Magnetic separation (rare earth magnets)", "Metal detection", "Prewash processing", "Retail and bulk packaging", "Food safety management (P.A.S.S. System)", "Supply chain management", "Grower partnership program", "Risk management"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Agriculture (dry beans)", "Food service", "Retail food", "Canning industry"], "materials": ["Pinto beans", "Great Northern beans", "Dry edible beans (various varieties)"], "equipment": ["Electric Eyes Machine (ESM Electric Sorting Machine)", "Cello-Pak retail packaging machine", "Round and slot hole screens", "Gravity machines", "De-stoner", "Electric eye sorter (optical sorter with front and rear cameras)", "Rare earth magnets", "Metal detection equipment", "Prewash machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee and family ownership since 1927", "Internally developed P.A.S.S. food safety system (GFSI aligned)", "Multiple GFSI-certified facilities with annual AIB audits", "Triple-clean processing with optical sorting and gravity separation", "Direct, multi-generational grower partnerships"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1927 as Chester B. Brown Co. -> /about", "Employee and family owned -> /", "Headquartered in Scottsbluff, Nebraska -> /", "Processes and sells dry edible beans -> /about", "Multiple GFSI certified facilities -> /quality", "P.A.S.S. System internally developed -> /quality", "Triple clean process with optical sorting -> /quality", "Acquisitions include ConAgra, Yellowstone Bean, etc. -> /about", "Fourth generation led by Kevin Kelley -> /about", "Electric Eyes Machine leased 1938 -> /about", "Cello-Pak machine 1946 -> /about", "Employee Stock Ownership Program 1983 -> /about", "Export to Cuba 2006 -> /about", "Equipment: round and slot hole screens, gravity machines, de-stoner, optical sorter, rare earth magnets, metal detection, prewash machines -> /quality", "Materials: Pinto beans, Great Northern beans -> /", "Ownership tags: Employee-owned, Family-owned -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "processes and sells the dry edible beans which are sourced directly from its local community of grower partnerships", "founded_year": "1927", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned", "Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kelley-bean-co-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='KeyStone Co-Pack Manufacturing operates from Pleasant Grove, Utah. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The firm provides turnkey contract manufacturing for nutritional supplements and personal care products. Services span ideation, formulation development, ingredient sourcing, production, packaging, and delivery. Production capabilities include powder blending and filling, capsule and tablet manufacturing, and gusseted bag filling. Packaging formats range from sticks, sachets, and tubs to bottles, jars, and vials. The company maintains a large inventory of hundreds of ingredients and employs R&D scientists to develop custom formulations. Fulfillment is coordinated through nearby partners.

KeyStone serves the food and beverage, health and wellness, and personal care and beauty sectors. Food and beverage clients include brands producing protein powders, baking mixes, and unpasteurized beverage shots. Health and wellness customers request protein blends, electrolytes, pre-workouts, and performance-enhancing powdered supplements. Personal care and beauty projects cover hair care, skincare, and oral care products.

